    <string name="info_dialog_title">How Detection Works</string>
    <string name="info_dialog_body">1. Magnetic Mount Detector: Many hidden vehicle GPS trackers use strong magnets. Your phone magnetometer measures magnetic flux in μT to spot hidden magnetic spikes (typically &gt; 85 μT).\n\n2. Bluetooth Tracker Scan: Scans nearby BLE advertisements to flag AirTag / Find My, Samsung SmartTag, Tile, and close-range wireless beacons.\n\n3. Device GPS Check: Verifies whether GPS hardware is installed on your device and reads live GNSS satellite signal strength (dB-Hz).\n\nNote: Passive cellular-only trackers with no magnet or Bluetooth radio cannot be directly detected by standard phone sensors.</string>
